  "breaking": [
    "One new database file, 004_web_inbox.sql (the web chat inbox table and a column for why a message went to another door). The update applies it and it is safe to run twice; a rollback does not undo it, so to go back past it restore the backup the update took.",
    "Meeting follow-ups no longer fall back to a built-in Notion database. Before updating, set NOTION_MEETINGS_DATA_SOURCE_ID in /etc/lares/keeper.json under defaultBindings[\"chief-of-staff\"].environment, or the meeting follow-up schedule stops with a clear message. Nothing else is affected.",
    "A message whose door is not connected now goes to web chat instead of being dropped."
  ]
